{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>YHWH, etc.</b> In their distress they sought You." "<b>צקון לחש.</b> The nun is added like the nun in אשר לא ידעון (Deuteronomy 8:3), and it is a strange word, and it should have been יצקו, therefore it comes without the alef of the root-verb, like והיום רד מאד (Judges 19:11), and the meaning is like ולפני יי ישפך שיחו (Psalms 102:1)." "And the meaning of <b>מוסרך</b> — that they would say in a whisper the chastisement with which You used to chastise them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:19.216942897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}